          "finish_reason": "length",
          "answer_excerpt": "# Technical Analysis of Plant Equipment Records: Failure Mode Assessment and Maintenance Recommendations\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\nThis report analyzes 18 equipment records spanning six asset classes (valves, scrubbers, heat exchangers, compressors, condensers, reactors, turbines, pipelines, and separators) across stations ranging from 5 to 359. The analysis identifies several units warranting immediate attention \u2014 most notably **compressor 9281** (178 \u00b0C discharge temperature, elevated vibration), **pipeline 3467** (165 \u00b0C with high flow and vibration), **condenser 9501** (161 \u00b0C, well outside normal condensing temperatures), and **valve 1132** (severely restricted flow of 9 m\u00b3/h against 452 kPa). A further cluster of units shows elevated vibration in the 6.5\u20137.7 mm/s band, which under ISO 10816/20816 guidance falls into the \"unsatisfactory for continuous operation\" zone and merits corrective planning.\n\nThe dataset also contains anomalies that suggest instrumentation or data-quality issues (e.g., pipeline 2077 at \u221211 \u00b0C), which are flagged separately because acting on bad data is as hazardous as ignoring good",
