          "finish_reason": "length",
          "answer_excerpt": "# Technical Analysis of Plant Equipment Records: Failure Modes, Key Measurements, and Maintenance Actions\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\nThis report analyzes 18 equipment records spanning six asset classes (pumps, reactors, condensers, turbines, valves, heat exchangers, scrubbers, separators, and compressors) across 17 stations. The dataset contains several anomalies that warrant immediate attention: a sub-zero temperature on an operating valve (Record 0000009), a condenser operating at 781 kPa with 8.1 mm/s vibration (Record 0000005), a turbine at 804 kPa with only 71% efficiency (Record 0000006), and a compressor running at 141\u00b0C with abnormally low vibration of 0.5 mm/s (Record 0000017), which may indicate a stalled or severely fouled machine rather than a healthy one.\n\nThe analysis below proceeds in three parts: (1) a fleet-wide statistical baseline, (2) asset-by-asset failure mode analysis with the measurements that matter most for each, and (3) a prioritized, concrete maintenance action list.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Fleet-Wide Statistical Baseline\n\nEstablishing a baseline from the dataset itself is essential before flag",
